title The ceiling and the header -- Comlink's payload bound takes a desk, and the compiler is handed the half a grep cannot read
prompt The standing Silence seat: open on ListAgents and the cold roster, reds first, council row N mod 5, QA on touch, twice-pulled send, path-limited signing, stop at custody gates.
think OTHER HAND BEFORE A FILE MOVED. ListAgents named one peer, grain-c0, interactive, eighteen hours old. HEAD sat on main, level with xy/main at 0/0, no rebase-merge directory, no stash, empty index -- the four readings %364 was booked for, taken before anything was read.
think REDS FIRST. reds_status_consistency_scan reports exactly one OPEN row, %360, and its remainder is the seed-subject spelling at custody gate %1 plus twenty-one red guards in lanes this seat does not hold. Nothing agent-doable there, so the door stayed the card's: Comlink's bounds, one desk against Tablecloth's four.
think ROTA. N=3833 by git rev-list --count HEAD gives row 3, WATER -- Venus, care and flow, sense taste, read up close by sipping the actual code. Its fixed seat is the happy zone and the thin edge, and it chose the shape of the whole lap: the pure heart proven by fast isolated witnesses, the unruly world pressed out to a thin edge. Its cardinal seat asks what smaller thing already works -- Tablecloth's four desks and their scan/control/witness trio -- and this grew from that rather than being designed fresh.
think THE CRUX, FOUND BY READING RATHER THAN BY THINKING. Comlink publishes 35 max_ constants and had one pedestal, and that pedestal shows a POLICY rather than a bound. The one worth the first desk is max_wire_payload=340, because it sizes real buffers, gates asserts, and two further bounds derive from it.
think THE MECHANISM. comlink/wire_format.rye DERIVES the ceiling: max_message = wire_capacity - off_cipher, where wire_capacity is a literal 528 and off_cipher is the end of a five-field offset chain. Three modules spell the answer 340 as a bare literal named max_wire_payload and cite no upstream room; a fourth, recall_batch_wire.rye, derives its own ceiling from one of those literals, so the copy propagates.
think ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN A RULE, WHICH IS %354's SHAPE ONE VANE OVER. I computed the header on metal with zig rather than by hand: 32 sender + 12 nonce + 64 name + 64 sig + 16 tag = 188, and 528 - 188 = 340. Only sender is a literal; the other four come from ChaCha20Poly1305, Sha3_512, and Kumara. So 340 equals 340 only because Ed25519 signs in 64 bytes -- and the card books Kumara moving to SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s, which moves off_tag, off_cipher, and max_message together.
think ONE MODULE ALREADY KNEW. comlink/rehearsal_wire.rye holds `comptime { assert(payload_max <= wf.max_message); }`. So of four payload-bounding modules, one proved the relation and three stated it in prose while spelling a literal -- recall_sync_wire.rye's own doc comment even names max_message and then writes 340 by hand.
think THE HONEST LIMIT DECIDED THE DESIGN. A shell scan can read text and can never evaluate ChaCha20Poly1305.nonce_length, so a scan alone could only ever prove the tie was WRITTEN. The compiler evaluates it. That is the thin edge doing the one job only it can do, so the repair is a comptime tie rather than a cleverer grep.
think PROVEN BOTH WAYS BEFORE IT SHIPPED. I planted the tie INVERTED first and required a refusal -- rye build-lib stopped at `called at comptime here` -- then flipped it true and required a build. A comptime block that is never evaluated would have passed the second test in perfect silence.
obs THE SYMLINK WAS THE LAP'S REAL SURPRISE, AND IT MOVED A LANE BOUNDARY. My edit through comlink/ landed in mantra/recall_sync_wire.rye, mantra/recall_tablecloth_query_wire.rye, and amphora/vessel_fetch_wire.rye -- comlink/ carries symlinks, and `git checkout -- comlink/<f>.rye` does not restore through one. Mantra is this seat's lane and Amphora is not, so I restored the Amphora file and left its room to its owner, named on the desk and on the card. Two rooms tied, the third named not touched.
obs THE TIE COUNT IS A FLOOR RATHER THAN AN EQUALITY, AND THAT IS THE POINT. A gate spelled `= 2` would red on Amphora's honest work the day they take their half, so the scan reads `ties_wired >= 2` and control case 25 proves a third room walking free. A guard that punishes a peer for finishing the job is a guard someone turns off.
obs THE SCAN CARRIES NO VALUE OF ITS OWN. It reads the desk's number, reads wire_capacity from the Rye, sums the header the desk lists, and compares -- so control case 23 raises the wire honestly in every room and WALKS FREE, which is the failure mode the elder Tend witnesses have: they grep the literal in both rooms and so red on a correct raise until a hand edits the guard.
obs THE SHARPEST CASE IS 15, AND IT IS WHY A LINK IS READ RATHER THAN VALUES COMPARED. Respell max_message as a literal 340 and every number in the scan still agrees -- desk 340, capacity minus header 340, all three literals 340 -- while the derivation is gone. Only a reading of the derivation itself sees it.
obs THE COMPOSITION IS READ, NOT A REMEMBERED 188. Case 24 widens a header field by four and raises capacity by four, landing the ceiling back on 340 by a different route, and walks free; case 11 swaps two offsets in the Rye, keeping every number and reshaping the envelope, and refuses on the names. The pinned line is the composition rather than the number, because no honest raise moves it.
obs ONE CONTROL CASE FAILED FIRST AND TAUGHT ITS OWN PLANT. Deleting the example line drops a placard keyword, so placard_wrong fired before example_missing and that reading was never proven from the failing side. The plant now spoils the VALUE and keeps the keyword. My expected counts were wrong beside it -- I wrote 19 refusals for 21 cases -- and the control caught my arithmetic rather than my reasoning.
obs ROSTERED, BECAUSE %360's CEILING ONLY FALLS. A new unrostered witness would have read unheard=1154 against a ceiling of 1153 and reddened unheard_guard. The row is seated in construction/standing-equipment.kyri at tier cadence, and the proof it is heard is arithmetic rather than a claim: the scan reads exactly 1153 with verdict=ok, which it could not if mine were unheard.
obs THE COLD ROSTER IS UNRUN AND I SAY SO RATHER THAN CLAIM IT. No full-green receipt exists on this bench, so --scoped refuses outright for want of a head to diff from, and the full pass has not closed under five hours here against forty minutes on grain-hush. What stands instead: the new witness GREEN on metal, the two witnesses whose watched files this round touched GREEN (tablecloth_glow_tend, unheard_guard), the card's own guards GREEN, and the roster's line-one probe clean.
obs THE ROSTER'S OWN WITNESS REFUSES, AND THE REASON IS NOT MINE. standing_equipment_scan reads runs_red=2 -- pond_enclosure_door and rule_twin -- both named on the card at gate %7. My row parses clean beside them: guards_unknown_tier=0, runs_unrostered=0, tier_cadence risen by one.
obs NINETEEN GUEST MODULES REFUSE TO BUILD ON THIS BENCH AND ALWAYS DID. `fence iorw, iorw` is a RISC-V instruction being assembled for arm64. I proved it predates the tie by stashing my change and reddening the same guest on the clean tree, rather than reporting a fault I had not attributed.
obs NOT BOOKED AS A RED, AND THE REASON IS THE LAW'S OWN WORDING. Nothing here produced a wrong answer: 340 equals 340 in every room today. A red is something wrong; a ratchet is something not yet uniform and books nothing. This was the second, so it is displayed, tied, and named on the card rather than given a ledger row.
