file src/shape/shape-comlink-wire-payload-bound.glow the vane's first bound desk -- 340 shown beside the 188-byte header it is the complement of
file tools/fixtures/c/comlink_glow_tend_scan.sh reads desk, capacity, composition, literals and ties apart; holds no value of its own
file tools/fixtures/c/comlink_glow_tend_control.sh 26 cases in a throwaway pen -- 21 refusals, 5 welcomes, every reading shown from both sides
file tools/fixtures/c/comlink_payload_tie_probe.sh the reading a grep cannot take -- the compiler asked twice, as written and inverted
file tools/co/comlink_glow_tend_witness.rish the rung: scan, pinned composition, control, metal tie, and the desk lowered through Glow
file mantra/recall_sync_wire.rye the comptime tie, so a payload ceiling can never outrun its wire
file mantra/recall_tablecloth_query_wire.rye the same tie, second of the two rooms this lane holds
file src/shape/README.md the roster row and the run line for the new rung
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri guard comlink_glow_tend at tier cadence, so %360's ceiling holds rather than rises
file tools/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_witness.rish its header said Comlink one in the present tense; now past, with the change since named
file construction/ITINERARY.md the door marked walked, Comlink's other bounds named next, Amphora's copy handed on, back under bound
recommend check-in (Claude) THE WORK IS GREEN AND ONE RULING IS WORTH YOUR WORD. max_wire_payload stands on a desk beside the header it completes, 26 pen cases prove the guard both ways, and the compiler now refuses a payload ceiling that outruns its wire -- proven by inverting the tie, not by asserting it. The ruling I would ask for is the lane boundary the symlinks drew: comlink/ reaches into mantra/ and amphora/, so a lap working "Comlink" can edit three rooms without noticing it left one. I tied the two Mantra rooms and left Amphora's, which is the cautious read -- yet the honest question is whether a symlinked file belongs to the room it lives in or the room it is reached through, and that answer is bigger than this lap. Two things above my hand stay named where they were: %360's seed-subject spelling is gate %1, and the roster's own auditor waits on gate %7. One bench fact unchanged from the last lap and worth your eye: with no receipt on disk this bench still has no affordable way to prove a full cold pass, so the roster directive is honest in name and out of reach here.
